        },
        {
          "id": "ready-meaning",
          "domain": "visual",
          "mode": "visual",
          "check": "Viewed alone, the image reads as successful completion (Ready) rather than activity, failure, pause, or the idle Start control.",
          "basis": "Consumer state mapping ok -> succeeded -> label Ready, while idle uses the Start vector. Brief: the working loop must not look like success, so Ready itself must convey success; the current update requires conveying successful completion. Judging Ready against the actual future Working/Retry/Paused images is deferred.",
          "scope": "This Ready candidate on its own, plus the already-existing Start vector.",
          "authority": "requirement",
          "sources": [
            {"path": "src/queue.ts", "locator": "stateAfter: ok -> succeeded", "lines": [3, 3]},
            {"path": "src/queue-view.ts", "locator": "idle: Start, assets/start.svg", "lines": [3, 3]},
            {"path": "src/queue-view.ts", "locator": "succeeded: label Ready", "lines": [6, 6]},
            {"path": "BRIEF.md", "locator": "The working loop must communicate activity without looking like success", "lines": [3, 3]},
            {"path": "BRIEF.md", "locator": "Current update: convey successful completion", "lines": [9, 9]},
            {"path": "assets/start.svg", "locator": "play-triangle path M4 2L14 8L4 14Z", "lines": [1, 1]}
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "readability-1x-3x",
          "domain": "visual",
          "mode": "visual",
          "check": "Composited on #172336, the silhouette is readable at 1x and at 3x nearest-neighbor scale, with no essential detail (including the asymmetry of the check-mark arms) lost into the panel colour.",
          "basis": "Owner brief requires readable silhouettes inspected at 1x and 3x nearest on the actual dark panel and the current update keeps the review display conditions; #172336 is the consumer-observed panel colour (display.background).",
          "scope": "This Ready candidate at the declared display conditions.",
          "authority": "requirement",
